     "type": "example",
     "title": "Day 3: Wednesday",
     "content": "**Day 3: Wednesday — Approaching the 30-Plant Mark**\n\nWednesday introduces seven new plants. By tonight you will be at 28 unique plants — just two short of the weekly target with four days still to go.\n\n**Breakfast (7:00 AM) — Asparagus and Mushroom Frittata**\n• Fibre first: Side of rocket (arugula) salad (two fists)\n• Protein: Frittata with asparagus, mushroom, and eggs (palm-sized wedge)\n• Fats: Fat from the eggs and cooking oil\n• Carbs last: Sourdough toast (1 slice)\n\n**Lunch (12:30 PM) — Roasted Cauliflower and Chickpea Bowl**\n• Fibre first: Roasted cauliflower florets (two fists)\n• Protein: Chickpeas tossed with the cauliflower (palm-sized)\n• Fats: Olive oil for roasting (thumb-sized)\n• Carbs last: Wild rice (cupped hand)\n\n**Dinner (5:30 PM) — Grilled Chicken with Steamed Vegetables**\n• Fibre first: Steamed zucchini and green beans (two fists)\n• Protein: Grilled chicken thigh (palm-sized)\n• Fats: Fat naturally in the chicken thigh\n• Carbs last: Sweet potato mash (cupped hand)\n\n**New plants today:** Rocket, asparagus, cauliflower, chickpea, wild rice, zucchini, green bean\n**Running total: 28 plants**",
