     "type": "example",
     "title": "Day 5: Friday",
     "content": "**Day 5: Friday — Adding More Diversity**\n\nFriday introduces pumpkin, eggplant, and pumpkin seeds. Lunch features a soup where the fibre is built into the meal — the pumpkin itself is the vegetable base.\n\n**Breakfast (7:00 AM) — Avocado and Eggs on Rye**\n• Fibre first: Cherry tomatoes on the side (two fists with the salad leaves)\n• Protein: Poached eggs (2 eggs, palm-sized)\n• Fats: Avocado slices (thumb-sized)\n• Carbs last: Rye toast (1 slice)\n\n**Lunch (12:30 PM) — Pumpkin Soup**\nFibre is built into this meal. The pumpkin soup base is the vegetable and fibre component.\n• Base: Pumpkin soup (fibre built in from the pumpkin)\n• Protein: Protein from the pumpkin and any added stock\n• Fats: Pumpkin seeds sprinkled on top (thumb-sized)\n• Carbs last: Sourdough bread on the side (cupped hand)\n\n**Dinner (5:30 PM) — Herb Chicken with Grilled Vegetables**\n• Fibre first: Grilled eggplant slices and roasted tomatoes (two fists)\n• Protein: Herb-crusted chicken breast (palm-sized)\n• Fats: Olive oil used for grilling (thumb-sized)\n• Carbs last: Couscous (cupped hand)\n\n**New plants today:** Pumpkin, pumpkin seed, eggplant\n**Running total: 37 plants**",
