     "explanation": "Research from the American Gut Project found that people who eat 30 or more different plant foods per week have significantly more diverse gut microbiomes than those eating fewer than 10. Each plant species contains unique types of fibre that feed different bacterial populations in your gut. Greater microbial diversity is consistently linked to better metabolic health, stronger immune function, and more stable blood glucose responses throughout the day.",
