     "type": "application",
     "title": "Building Your Personal Cardio Engine",
     "content": "Use this checklist to launch your aerobic programme this week:\n\nChoose your Zone 2 activity. Pick one from: brisk walking, cycling, swimming, or elliptical. You can mix them, but start with one you will actually do.\n\nSchedule 2-3 sessions this week. Put them in your calendar with a specific time. Treat them like appointments.\n\nSet a duration. Start with 20 minutes if you are new to regular cardio. Build toward 30-40 minutes over the first few weeks (Lesson 12 progression principles apply).\n\nDo the talk test in your first session. Find the pace where you can speak full sentences but notice your breathing. Note this pace for reference.\n\nFrom Week 3, decide: full 4x4 intervals, 30-second surges, or stick with Zone 2 only. All three options are valid.\n\n⚠️ If you take insulin or sulfonylureas: test blood glucose before starting. Have fast-acting glucose accessible. Consider reducing insulin dose in consultation with your healthcare team. Stop if you feel symptoms of hypoglycaemia (shakiness, sweating, confusion).",
