     "explanation": "The programme alternates A and B sessions, and Week 3 adds Zone 2 cardio. With three training days, the cleanest approach is one A, one B, and one Zone 2, spread across the week with rest days between. Doing B three times ignores the rotation principle, skipping strength removes the glucose-sink benefit, and combining sessions into one marathon defeats the purpose of manageable volume. The daily walk continues regardless.",
