     "explanation": "The protocol requires three days between reintroductions so you can attribute any reaction to the correct food. With seven days, you can test on Day 22, observe for two days, then test the second on Day 25 and observe through Day 27. That leaves the third item for the next week. Testing all three at once makes it impossible to know which caused a reaction, and testing on consecutive days does not leave observation time.",
